This license applies to the tPoseidon source code, release packages,
documentation and any other material published by the tPoseidon project
(together, "the Software") during the beta phase. It is not an open-source
license. The project intends to release the Software under an open-source
license after the beta; until it does, these terms apply.

1. Definitions

   "You" means the person or organisation using the Software.

   "Official Release" means a release package published by the tPoseidon
   project on its official release page, unmodified.

   "Community Use" means running the Software for yourself, your friends or
   a community of players without charging for access to it.

   "Derived Work" means any work that copies, modifies, translates, ports or
   is based on the Software or any part of it, including forks and other
   emulators built from it.

2. What you may do

   Free of charge, you may:

   a. download Official Releases and install them on any number of your own
      machines;

   b. run Official Releases and host game servers with them for Community
      Use, including servers open to the public over the internet;

   c. change the Software's configuration through the settings, files and
      tools the Software provides for that purpose;

   d. read the source code, build it and change it on your own machines,
      only to test it, to study it, or to prepare bug reports and
      suggestions to the tPoseidon project under section 4;

   e. report bugs, request features and take part in the project's issue
      tracker, forum and other spaces.

3. What you may not do

   Unless the tPoseidon project gives you written permission, you may not:

   a. publish, distribute, upload or otherwise make available the Software,
      in source or binary form, anywhere other than through the official
      project pages (link to the official release page instead);

   b. create, publish, distribute or host a Derived Work, including a fork,
      a modified release package or another emulator based on the
      Software;

   c. host a game server with a modified build of the Software, except
      privately on your own machines for the purposes in section 2(d);

   d. sell the Software, sell access to a server running it, or sell items,
      characters or advantages in a game hosted with it;

   e. remove or change any copyright, license or notice in the Software;

   f. use the Software or the project's spaces to distribute the game
      client or any file belonging to the game.

   If the Software is hosted on a service whose terms let users fork or copy
   repositories (for example by pressing a "Fork" button), you may use that
   feature only to the extent the service's terms require, and only to view
   the Software and to send bug reports and suggestions back to the tPoseidon
   project. Using,
   building for distribution, hosting or distributing such a copy is not
   permitted.

4. Contributions

   You may send bug reports and suggestions to the tPoseidon project.
   Code contributions (patches and pull requests) are not accepted until
   the project's 1.0 release. By sending anything to the project you:

   a. confirm that you wrote it or otherwise have the right to submit it,
      and that it does not contain files belonging to the game or code you
      are not allowed to share;

   b. grant the tPoseidon project a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive,
      royalty-free, irrevocable license to use, copy, modify, distribute and
      sublicense your contribution as part of the Software, under this
      license, under any later version of it, and under any open-source
      license the project later adopts.

5. The game and its assets

   tPoseidon is an independent server emulator. The game it works with, its
   client, art, music, maps, data, names and trademarks belong to their
   respective owners. None of them are included in the Software or licensed
   by this license. You must obtain the game client yourself and use it in
   line with the rights you have to it. See the NOTICE file.

6. Termination

   If you break these terms, your rights under this license end
   automatically. If you stop the breach within 30 days of being told about
   it, your rights are restored, unless you have been told about a breach of
   these terms before.

